// womb/lang/hello.vuma — Minimal VUMA 2.0 hello-world program
// Prints 42 to stdout and exits 0.
//
// This is the bootstrap milestone target: a minimal program that
// exercises the bootstrap compiler's full pipeline (lex → parse →
// AST → IR → x86_64 codegen → ELF64) end-to-end.
//
// The bootstrap compiler (womb/lang/{full_lexer,full_parser,ir_builder,
// codegen,elf}.vuma) supports a V1.0-era grammar subset (fn, let, if,
// while, print_int, return, integer literals, binary ops, allocate/free
// interception). VUMA 2.0 PMT constructs (layout, state_new, field
// access, transforms) are not yet supported by the bootstrap's lexer/
// parser/IR-builder/codegen — extending the bootstrap to compile full
// PMT source is future work (see Phase 3d worklog entry).
//
// The 5 bootstrap FILES themselves have been ported to PMT (no V1.0
// pointer syntax) — they compile cleanly under VUMA 2.0 PMT-only mode.
// This hello.vuma uses only the bootstrap's supported subset so the
// self-host test can verify the ported bootstrap still emits a working
// x86_64 ELF that prints "42".

fn main() -> i32 {
    print_int(42);
    return 0;
}
